@using Microsoft.Extensions.Options
@using Glosify.Services.Legal
@inject IOptions<LegalOptions> Legal
@{
    Layout = "~/Views/Shared/_GlosifyLayout.cshtml";
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
    ViewData["Description"] = "How Glosify and the Glosify Live Subtitles Chrome extension handle personal data.";
    var legal = Legal.Value;
}

<main class="auth-shell legal-shell">
    <article class="glass-card legal-document">
        <header class="auth-card-header">
            <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
            <p>Last updated 10 August 2026</p>
        </header>

        <h2>Who controls your data</h2>
        <p><strong>@legal.ControllerName</strong> operates Glosify and is the controller for personal data described here. Contact <a href="mailto:@legal.ContactEmail">@legal.ContactEmail</a> for privacy or deletion requests.</p>

        <h2>Data Glosify handles</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Account information such as email address, internal account ID, authentication method, and Google or Microsoft external-login identifiers.</li>
            <li>Language preferences, quizzes, learning content, credits, reservations, usage transactions, and session metadata needed to provide and protect the service.</li>
            <li>For live subtitles, audio from the tab you explicitly choose, translated captions, target language, timing, and connection diagnostics.</li>
            <li>If you separately enable transcript saving, finalized original-language speech, transcript titles, timestamps, and the selected learning language.</li>
            <li>Security and operational metadata such as IP address, request time, status, and error diagnostics. Application logs are designed not to contain tab audio or caption text.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Live subtitles and Microsoft processing</h2>
        <p>Chrome captures audio only after you press <strong>Start subtitles</strong> for the active tab. The audio is streamed through Glosify to Microsoft Foundry for real-time speech processing and translation. Tab audio is not written to Glosify storage. Captions are displayed in the tab and kept transiently unless you separately opt in to transcript saving.</p>
        <p>Microsoft processes the stream and related service metadata as Glosify's cloud provider. Google and Microsoft process information under their own policies when you choose their OAuth sign-in services.</p>

        <h2>Purposes and legal basis</h2>
        <p>Glosify uses this data to authenticate you, deliver requested learning and subtitle features, maintain your content, administer credits and the application budget, prevent abuse, troubleshoot failures, and comply with legal obligations. Processing is necessary to provide the service you request and for legitimate security and reliability interests; optional transcript storage is based on your explicit choice.</p>

        <h2>Storage, retention, and deletion</h2>
        <p>Transcript saving is off by default. When enabled, the finalized original speech is stored in your private Glosify account until you delete the transcript or account. Account content and credit records are retained while the account is active and as long as reasonably required for security, accounting, dispute handling, or legal obligations. Cloud backup and operational-log copies expire under the configured Microsoft Azure retention schedules rather than disappearing immediately.</p>
        <p>You can delete saved transcripts from the Transcripts page and use the account-management deletion tools after signing in. You may also contact the address above. Deleting content does not revoke an OAuth provider's own copy; manage that relationship with Google or Microsoft as well.</p>

        <h2>Chrome extension data</h2>
        <p>The extension stores the minimum local settings and authentication material needed to stay connected, such as language choices, session state, and Glosify bearer tokens. It uses active-tab, tab-capture, offscreen, scripting, storage, identity, and glosify.se access only to connect the account and place translated subtitles over the tab the user starts.</p>

        <h2>Chrome Web Store Limited Use</h2>
        <p>Glosify's use and transfer of information received from Google APIs will adhere to the Chrome Web Store User Data Policy, including the Limited Use requirements. Glosify does not sell extension user data, use it for personalised advertising, or transfer it for unrelated credit or lending purposes.</p>

        <h2>Changes and questions</h2>
        <p>Material changes will be published on this page with a new effective date. For questions, access, correction, portability, objection, or deletion requests, contact <a href="mailto:@legal.ContactEmail">@legal.ContactEmail</a>.</p>

        <nav class="legal-links" aria-label="Legal pages">
            <a asp-action="Terms">Terms of Service</a>
            <a asp-action="Support">Support</a>
        </nav>
    </article>
</main>
